/-!
# Kernels of surjections onto finitely presented sheaves of modules

Let `R` be a sheaf of rings on a site. Stacks Tag 01BP says that if `F` is a sheaf of
`R`-modules of finite presentation and `θ : G ⟶ F` is a surjection with `G` of finite type,
then `Ker θ` is of finite type. The argument is local: over a small enough object one picks a
presentation `free m ⟶ free n ⟶ F` of `F`, lifts the generators of `G` through `free n ⟶ F`
to get `α`, lifts the generators of `free n` through `θ` to get `β`, and then
`(χ ≫ β, γ - α ≫ β)` surjects onto `Ker θ`.

This file develops that argument. The content is organised so that each ingredient is a
statement about an existing Mathlib construction:

* restriction of a sheaf of modules to a slice site preserves kernels;
* global sections of such a restriction are the sections over the object one restricted to;
* a global section of the target of an epimorphism lifts after passing to a covering family;
* the comparison morphism of the Stacks argument has the surjection as its cokernel, so its
  source generates the kernel.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.sectionsEquivOfTerminal` identifies the global
  sections of a sheaf of modules on a site with a terminal object with its sections at that
  object.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.sectionsOverEquiv` is the special case of a
  restriction to a slice site: `(M.over V).sections ≃ M.val.obj (op V)`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.unitOverIso` records that restriction to a slice
  site takes the unit sheaf to the unit sheaf.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.cmp` is the comparison morphism
  `free m ⨿ free Iγ ⟶ A` built from the presentation and the two comparison maps `α` and `β`
  of the Stacks 01BP argument.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.localGeneratorsDataOfGeneratingSections` reads global
  generating sections as local generators data for the trivial covering of the site.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.preservesLimitOverFunctor`: restriction to a slice
  site preserves limits of small shape; in particular it preserves kernels. This is what
  identifies `(kernel θ).over V` with `kernel (θ.over V)`, and it is not available in Mathlib:
  neither `PresheafOfModules.pushforward` nor `SheafOfModules.pushforward` carries a
  `PreservesFiniteLimits` instance there.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.exists_lift_over_of_epi`: a global section of the
  target of an epimorphism of sheaves of modules lifts along that epimorphism after
  restriction to the members of a covering sieve. This is the local lifting step of the Stacks
  argument, and it is where `epi_iff_isLocallySurjective` is used.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.epi_kernelLift_of_isColimit`: in an abelian
  category, if `g` is a cokernel of `f` then the induced morphism `X ⟶ kernel g` is an
  epimorphism.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.isColimitCmp`: the mathematical heart of Stacks
  01BP. Given a presentation `free m --χ--> free n --φ--> F`, an epimorphism
  `γ : free Iγ ⟶ A`, a morphism `ψ : A ⟶ F` and comparison maps `α : free Iγ ⟶ free n`,
  `β : free n ⟶ A` with `α ≫ φ = γ ≫ ψ` and `β ≫ ψ = φ`, the morphism `ψ` is a cokernel of
  `cmp χ γ α β`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.generatingSectionsKernel`: consequently `kernel ψ`
  is generated by `m ⊕ Iγ` sections. For finite `m` and `Iγ` this is the local form of Stacks
  01BP.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.iInf_mem`: a finite infimum of covering sieves is
  covering, used to intersect the finitely many covering sieves produced by the lifting step.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.isFiniteType_kernel_of_presentation`: **Stacks 01BP
  for a sheaf of modules admitting a finite presentation by global sections.** If `F` has such
  a presentation and `θ : G ⟶ F` is an epimorphism from a sheaf of modules generated by
  finitely many global sections, then `Ker θ` is of finite type.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.isFiniteType_kernel_free_of_presentation`: the same
  statement for `ψ : free I ⟶ F` with `I` finite, which is part (1) of Stacks 01BP in the
  globally presented case.

## Scope: what is *not* proved here

Stacks 01BP is stated for `F` of finite presentation and `G` of finite type in the *local*
senses `SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation` and `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, i.e. for data
that exists only after passing to a covering family. The theorems above assume instead that
the presentation of `F` and the generators of `G` are global.

The reduction of the local statement to the global one is not carried out here, and the reason
is structural rather than incidental. The lifting step `exists_lift_over_of_epi` lifts a
section along an epimorphism *of the ambient site*, producing the lift over objects of that
same site. When the presentation of `F` only exists over a member `Y` of a covering family,
the epimorphism `free n ⟶ F.over Y` lives on the slice site over `Y`, so the lifting step runs
there and produces its lifts over objects of `Over Y` — that is, in the twice-sliced category
`SheafOfModules ((R.over Y).over Z)`. Closing the gap therefore needs one of:

* a `LocalGeneratorsData` analogue of `SheafOfModules.QuasicoherentData.bind`, together with
  `HasSheafify ((J.over X).over Z) AddCommGrpCat.{u}` and the corresponding
  `WEqualsLocallyBijective` for all `X` and `Z`, so that `isFiniteType_kernel_of_presentation`
  can be instantiated on each slice site and the results glued; or
* a slice-relative form of `exists_lift_over_of_epi`, lifting along an epimorphism of sheaves
  on `Over Y` but landing in `SheafOfModules (R.over V)` for objects `V` of `C` with a map to
  `Y`, via `SheafOfModules.overMap` and `SheafOfModules.overFunctorMap`. This avoids the
  twice-sliced instances but needs `HasPullbacks C`, which is what makes `overMap` a left
  adjoint and hence colimit preserving.

## Implementation notes

The 01BP argument is run by universal property rather than by chasing sections. Writing `ψ` as
the cokernel of the comparison morphism is an elementary computation with `coprod.desc` and
`Preadditive.sub_comp`, and `epi_kernelLift_of_isColimit` then turns that cokernel statement
into the surjectivity of `free (m ⊕ Iγ) ⟶ kernel ψ`. Doing it this way avoids needing
`Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective` anywhere except in the one place where it is genuinely the
content, namely `exists_lift_over_of_epi`.

Nothing here specialises a universe. The site `C : Type u₁` has `Category.{v₁} C` and the
sheaf of rings is `R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}`, with `u`, `u₁`, `v₁` unrelated, which is the
generality in which Mathlib states `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` and
`SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation`.

The abelian structure on `SheafOfModules.{u} R` needs `HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}` and
`J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}`; `HasWeakSheafify` is *not* enough, since
`Abelian (SheafOfModules.{u} R)` is transferred along the sheafification adjunction and so
needs sheafification to be left exact. Consequently every statement here that takes a kernel,
a cokernel or a biproduct of sheaves of modules on a *slice* site carries
`HasSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}` rather than the weaker hypothesis which suffices
merely to *state* `IsFiniteType`.

What `SheafOfModules.Presentation.map` and `SheafOfModules.mapFreeIso` require is that
restriction to a slice site preserve colimits, and that is what is assumed here. Mathlib gets it
from `HasBinaryProducts C`, which makes the restriction a left adjoint
(`SheafOfModules.overPushforwardOverAdj`); that derivation is kept as
`preservesColimitsOverFunctor`, so a site with binary products — the site of opens of a
topological space, which is the case Stacks 01BP is stated for — satisfies the hypothesis by
instance search. Assuming the conclusion instead of the products is what lets a site with no
finite limits use this file, which is what Stacks Tag 082T needs.

The identification `(unit R).over V = unit (R.over V)` is definitional, and so are the two
compatibility lemmas for `sectionsOverEquiv`; `unitOverIso` is `Iso.refl`. This is why
`exists_lift_over_of_epi` is short.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01AH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01AH)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite SheafOfModules

universe u v₁ u₁ u₂ v₂

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel

/-! ### Finite infima of covering sieves -/

section Sieves

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)

/-- A finite infimum of covering sieves is covering. -/
lemma finsetInf_mem {U : C} {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι) (S : ι → Sieve U)
    (hS : ∀ i ∈ s, S i ∈ J U) : s.inf S ∈ J U := by
  classical
  induction s using Finset.induction with
  | empty => simp [J.top_mem U]
  | insert i s _ ih =>
      rw [Finset.inf_insert]
      exact J.intersection_covering (hS i (by simp))
        (ih fun j hj => hS j (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hj))

/-- An infimum of covering sieves indexed by a finite type is covering. -/
lemma iInf_mem {U : C} {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (S : ι → Sieve U) (hS : ∀ i, S i ∈ J U) :
    (⨅ i, S i) ∈ J U := by
  classical
  cases nonempty_fintype ι
  rw [← Finset.inf_univ_eq_iInf]
  exact finsetInf_mem J _ S fun i _ => hS i

/-- An arrow lies in an infimum of sieves exactly when it lies in each of them. -/
lemma iInf_apply {U : C} {ι : Type*} (S : ι → Sieve U) {V : C} (g : V ⟶ U) :
    (⨅ i, S i) g ↔ ∀ i, (S i) g := by
  rw [iInf, Sieve.sInf_apply]
  exact ⟨fun h i => h (S i) ⟨i, rfl⟩, by rintro h S' ⟨i, rfl⟩; exact h i⟩

end Sieves

/-! ### Restriction to a slice site preserves limits -/

section Pushforward

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D]

/-- The pushforward of presheaves of modules along a functor preserves limits of small shape:
limits of presheaves of modules are computed pointwise, and pushforward is precomposition
followed by restriction of scalars. -/
@[sga "4 I 5.8.3" "Clause 1, special case"]
theorem preservesLimitPushforwardPresheaf {F : C ⥤ D} {S : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}}
    {R : Dᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}} (φ : S ⟶ F.op ⋙ R) {K : Type} [SmallCategory K]
    (G : K ⥤ PresheafOfModules.{u} R) :
    PreservesLimit G (PresheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} φ) where
  preserves {c} hc := ⟨by
    refine PresheafOfModules.evaluationJointlyReflectsLimits _ _ fun X => ?_
    have : PreservesLimit G (PresheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} φ ⋙
        PresheafOfModules.evaluation S X) := by
      show PreservesLimit G (PresheafOfModules.evaluation R (F.op.obj X) ⋙
        ModuleCat.restrictScalars (RingCat.Hom.hom (φ.app X)))
      infer_instance
    exact isLimitOfPreserves (PresheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} φ ⋙
      PresheafOfModules.evaluation S X) hc⟩

variable {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {K : GrothendieckTopology D} {F : C ⥤ D}
  {S : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}} {R : Sheaf K RingCat.{u}} [Functor.IsContinuous F J K]

/-- The pushforward of sheaves of modules along a continuous functor preserves limits of small
shape. In particular it preserves kernels. -/
instance preservesLimitPushforward
    (φ : S ⟶ (F.sheafPushforwardContinuous RingCat.{u} J K).obj R)
    {Kc : Type} [SmallCategory Kc] (G : Kc ⥤ SheafOfModules.{u} R) :
    PreservesLimit G (SheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} φ) := by
  have := preservesLimitPushforwardPresheaf (F := F) (S := S.obj) (R := R.obj) φ.hom
    (G ⋙ SheafOfModules.forget R)
  have : PreservesLimit G (SheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} φ ⋙ SheafOfModules.forget S) := by
    change PreservesLimit G (SheafOfModules.forget R ⋙ PresheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} φ.hom)
    exact comp_preservesLimit _ _
  exact preservesLimit_of_reflects_of_preserves _ (SheafOfModules.forget S)

end Pushforward

/-! ### Global sections over a slice site -/

section Sections

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}

/-- Global sections of a sheaf of modules on a site with a terminal object are its sections at
that object. -/
noncomputable def sectionsEquivOfTerminal {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D]
    {K : GrothendieckTopology D} {S : Sheaf K RingCat.{u}} (X : SheafOfModules.{u} S) {T : D}
    (hT : IsTerminal T) : X.sections ≃ X.val.obj (op T) where
  toFun s := s.val (op T)
  invFun x := PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk (M := X.val)
    (fun Z => X.val.map ((hT.from Z.unop).op) x) fun {Z Z'} g => by
      rw [← PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply]
      exact PresheafOfModules.congr_map_apply X.val
        (Quiver.Hom.unop_inj (hT.hom_ext _ _)) x
  left_inv s := by
    ext Z
    exact s.property ((hT.from Z.unop).op)
  right_inv x := by
    change X.val.map ((hT.from T).op) x = x
    rw [hT.hom_ext (hT.from T) (𝟙 T), op_id, X.val.map_id]
    rfl

/-- Global sections of the restriction of `M` to the slice site over `V` are the sections of
`M` over `V`. -/
noncomputable def sectionsOverEquiv (M : SheafOfModules.{u} R) (V : C) :
    (M.over V).sections ≃ M.val.obj (op V) where
  toFun s := s.val (op (Over.mk (𝟙 V)))
  invFun x := PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk (M := (M.over V).val)
    (fun Z => M.val.map (Z.unop.hom.op) x) fun {Z Z'} g => by
      change M.val.map (g.unop.left.op) (M.val.map (Z.unop.hom.op) x) = _
      rw [← PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply, ← op_comp, Over.w]
  left_inv s := by
    ext Z
    change M.val.map (Z.unop.hom.op) (s.val (op (Over.mk (𝟙 V)))) = _
    exact s.property ((Over.homMk Z.unop.hom (by simp) : Z.unop ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 V))).op
  right_inv x := by
    change M.val.map ((𝟙 V).op) x = x
    rw [op_id, M.val.map_id]
    rfl

/-- `sectionsOverEquiv` is natural in the sheaf of modules. -/
lemma sectionsOverEquiv_sectionsMap {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (f : M ⟶ N) (V : C)
    (s : (M.over V).sections) :
    sectionsOverEquiv N V (SheafOfModules.sectionsMap (f.over V) s) =
      f.val.app (op V) (sectionsOverEquiv M V s) := rfl

/-- The restriction to the slice site over `V` of a global section of `M`, read through
`sectionsOverEquiv`, is the value of that section at `V`. -/
lemma sectionsOverEquiv_unitHomEquiv {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (V : C)
    (σ : unit R ⟶ M) :
    sectionsOverEquiv M V ((M.over V).unitHomEquiv
        (show unit (R.over V) ⟶ M.over V from σ.over V)) =
      (M.unitHomEquiv σ).val (op V) := rfl

end Sections

/-! ### Local lifting along an epimorphism -/

section Lifting

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- A global section of the target of an epimorphism of sheaves of modules lifts along that
epimorphism after restriction to the members of a covering sieve. This is the "after shrinking
`U`" step of the Stacks 01BP argument. -/
theorem exists_lift_over_of_epi {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (p : M ⟶ N) [Epi p]
    (σ : unit R ⟶ N) (U : C) :
    ∃ S : Sieve U, S ∈ J U ∧ ∀ ⦃W : C⦄ (g : W ⟶ U), S g →
      ∃ τ : unit (R.over W) ⟶ M.over W,
        τ ≫ p.over W = (show unit (R.over W) ⟶ N.over W from σ.over W) := by
  refine ⟨Presheaf.imageSieve ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R.obj).map p.val)
      ((N.unitHomEquiv σ).val (op U)),
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.imageSieve_mem_of_epi p _, ?_⟩
  intro W g hg
  obtain ⟨y₀, hy⟩ := hg
  let y : M.val.obj (op W) := y₀
  have hy' : p.val.app (op W) y = N.val.map g.op ((N.unitHomEquiv σ).val (op U)) := hy
  refine ⟨(M.over W).unitHomEquiv.symm ((sectionsOverEquiv M W).symm y), ?_⟩
  apply (N.over W).unitHomEquiv.injective
  apply (sectionsOverEquiv N W).injective
  rw [SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv_comp_apply, Equiv.apply_symm_apply,
    sectionsOverEquiv_sectionsMap, Equiv.apply_symm_apply, sectionsOverEquiv_unitHomEquiv,
    ← PresheafOfModules.sections_property (N.unitHomEquiv σ) g.op]
  exact hy'

end Lifting

/-! ### Restriction to a slice site is colimit preserving -/

section OverFunctor

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C]
  {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}

/-- Restriction to a slice site takes the unit sheaf to the unit sheaf, on the nose. -/
noncomputable def unitOverIso (V : C) :
    unit (R.over V) ≅ (overFunctor.{u} R V).obj (unit R) := Iso.refl _

/-- The forward map of `unitOverIso V` is the identity. -/
@[simp] lemma unitOverIso_hom (V : C) : (unitOverIso (R := R) V).hom = 𝟙 _ := rfl

/-- The inverse map of `unitOverIso V` is the identity. -/
@[simp] lemma unitOverIso_inv (V : C) : (unitOverIso (R := R) V).inv = 𝟙 _ := rfl

/-- **Restriction of sheaves of modules to a slice site preserves limits of small shape**, hence
kernels. This is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel.preservesLimitPushforward` stated for
`SheafOfModules.overFunctor`, which is a `def` and so is not seen by instance search: limits of
sheaves of modules are computed objectwise and restriction only reindexes the objects.

Nothing here needs a hypothesis on the site. The original `preservesLimitOverFunctor` in the
`Main` section sits under that section's five instance binders — sheafifiability and local
bijectivity on `J` and on every slice, and `PreservesColimitsOfSize (overFunctor R V)` — none of
which its proof uses, and the last of which is available only through `HasBinaryProducts C` or an
adjunction, so it does not fire where it is wanted. This instance is stated at the hypotheses it
actually has. -/
noncomputable instance preservesLimit_overFunctor (V : C) {Kc : Type} [SmallCategory Kc]
    (G : Kc ⥤ SheafOfModules.{u} R) :
    PreservesLimit G (overFunctor.{u} R V) := by
  change PreservesLimit G (SheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} (𝟙 (R.over V)))
  infer_instance

/-- Restriction of sheaves of modules to a slice site preserves limits of any small shape; in
particular the countable products of shape `Discrete ℕ`.

That is the form the derived category consumes. It makes the Milnor triangle of an inverse system
of `D(𝒪)` restrict to the Milnor triangle of the restricted system, which is how derived
completeness along a sheaf of ideals — a condition on the slice site over each object of the
site — can be tested on a derived limit. -/
noncomputable instance preservesLimitsOfShapeOverFunctor (V : C) (Kc : Type) [SmallCategory Kc] :
    PreservesLimitsOfShape Kc (overFunctor.{u} R V) where

section Products

variable [HasBinaryProducts C]

/-- Restriction of sheaves of modules to a slice site is a left adjoint. This is
`SheafOfModules.overPushforwardOverAdj` stated for `SheafOfModules.overFunctor`, which is a
`def` and so is not seen by instance search. -/
noncomputable instance isLeftAdjointOverFunctor (V : C) :
    (overFunctor.{u} R V).IsLeftAdjoint := by
  change (SheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} (𝟙 (R.over V))).IsLeftAdjoint
  infer_instance

/-- Restriction of sheaves of modules to a slice site preserves colimits. This is what
`SheafOfModules.Presentation.map` and `SheafOfModules.mapFreeIso` need. A site with binary
products has it for this reason; a site without them can still have it, which is why the
statements below assume the conclusion rather than this hypothesis. -/
noncomputable instance preservesColimitsOverFunctor (V : C) :
    PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (overFunctor.{u} R V) :=
  (Adjunction.ofIsLeftAdjoint (overFunctor.{u} R V)).leftAdjoint_preservesColimits

end Products

variable [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ X : C, HasSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ X : C, (J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : C, PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (overFunctor.{u} R V)]

/-- The tautological sections of the free sheaf of modules on the slice site over `V` restrict
to the tautological sections of the restriction of the free sheaf of modules. -/
@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
lemma ιFree_mapFreeIso_over_hom {I : Type u} (V : C) (i : I) :
    ιFree i ≫ (mapFreeIso (overFunctor R V) I (unitOverIso V)).hom =
      (overFunctor R V).map (ιFree i) := by
  rw [ιFree_mapFreeIso_hom]
  exact Category.id_comp _


end OverFunctor

/-! ### Morphisms out of a free sheaf of modules -/

section Free

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- The component at `i` of the morphism out of `free I` attached to a family of sections. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma ιFree_freeHomEquiv_symm {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {I : Type u}
    (s : I → M.sections) (i : I) :
    ιFree i ≫ (freeHomEquiv M).symm s = M.unitHomEquiv.symm (s i) := by
  rw [← unitHomEquiv_symm_freeHomEquiv_apply, Equiv.apply_symm_apply]

/-- Two morphisms out of a free sheaf of modules agree as soon as they agree on the
tautological sections. -/
lemma free_hom_ext {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {I : Type u} {f g : free I ⟶ M}
    (h : ∀ i, ιFree i ≫ f = ιFree i ≫ g) : f = g :=
  (freeHomEquiv M).injective (funext fun i => by
    show M.unitHomEquiv (ιFree i ≫ f) = M.unitHomEquiv (ιFree i ≫ g)
    rw [h i])

end Free

/-! ### The kernel of a cokernel projection is the image -/

section Abelian

/-- In an abelian category, if `g` exhibits its target as a cokernel of `f`, then the morphism
`X ⟶ kernel g` induced by `f` is an epimorphism: the kernel of `g` is the image of `f`. -/
lemma epi_kernelLift_of_isColimit {A : Type*} [Category* A] [Abelian A] {X Y Z : A}
    (f : X ⟶ Y) (g : Y ⟶ Z) (H : f ≫ g = 0) (H' : IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ g H)) :
    Epi (kernel.lift g f H) := by
  let e : cokernel f ≅ Z := (H'.coconePointUniqueUpToIso (colimit.isColimit _)).symm
  have he : cokernel.π f ≫ e.hom = g := by simp [e]
  let h' : Abelian.image f ≅ kernel g :=
    kernel.mapIso (cokernel.π f) g (Iso.refl _) e (by simp [he])
  have comp_aux : Abelian.factorThruImage f ≫ h'.hom = kernel.lift g f H :=
    equalizer.hom_ext (by simp [h'])
  rw [← comp_aux]
  infer_instance

end Abelian

/-! ### The Stacks 01BP comparison morphism -/

section Cmp

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  {F A : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {m n Iγ : Type u}
  (χ : free (R := R) m ⟶ free (R := R) n) (γ : free (R := R) Iγ ⟶ A)
  (α : free (R := R) Iγ ⟶ free (R := R) n) (β : free (R := R) n ⟶ A)

/-- The comparison morphism `free m ⨿ free Iγ ⟶ A` of the Stacks 01BP argument. Here `χ` is
the relations map of a presentation of `F`, `γ` generates `A`, and `α`, `β` are the two
comparison maps between `ψ : A ⟶ F` and the presentation. -/
noncomputable def cmp : (free (R := R) m) ⨿ (free (R := R) Iγ) ⟶ A :=
  coprod.desc (χ ≫ β) (γ - α ≫ β)

/-- The comparison morphism `cmp χ γ α β` restricts to `χ ≫ β` on the summand `free m`. -/
@[reassoc] lemma inl_cmp : coprod.inl ≫ cmp χ γ α β = χ ≫ β := by
  simp only [cmp, coprod.inl_desc]

/-- The comparison morphism `cmp χ γ α β` restricts to `γ - α ≫ β` on the summand `free Iγ`. -/
@[reassoc] lemma inr_cmp : coprod.inr ≫ cmp χ γ α β = γ - α ≫ β := by
  simp only [cmp, coprod.inr_desc]

variable (φ : free (R := R) n ⟶ F) (ψ : A ⟶ F)
  (hχφ : χ ≫ φ = 0) (hα : α ≫ φ = γ ≫ ψ) (hβ : β ≫ ψ = φ)

include hχφ hα hβ in
/-- The comparison morphism lands in the kernel of `ψ`. -/
lemma cmp_comp : cmp χ γ α β ≫ ψ = 0 := by
  refine coprod.hom_ext ?_ ?_ <;> simp only [inl_cmp_assoc, inr_cmp_assoc, comp_zero]
  · rw [hβ, hχφ]
  · rw [Preadditive.sub_comp, Category.assoc, hβ, hα, sub_self]

include hχφ hα hβ in
/-- **The heart of Stacks 01BP.** `ψ` is a cokernel of the comparison morphism. Given a
morphism `h` killing `cmp χ γ α β`, the relation `γ ≫ h = α ≫ β ≫ h` lets one descend
`β ≫ h` through the presentation of `F`, and the resulting morphism `F ⟶ Z` is the required
factorisation; uniqueness holds because `ψ` is an epimorphism. -/
noncomputable def isColimitCmp (hcolim : IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ φ hχφ)) [Epi γ] [Epi φ] :
    IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ ψ (cmp_comp χ γ α β φ ψ hχφ hα hβ)) := by
  have hψ : Epi ψ := by
    have : Epi (β ≫ ψ) := by
      rw [hβ]
      infer_instance
    exact epi_of_epi β ψ
  have key : ∀ s : CokernelCofork (cmp χ γ α β),
      χ ≫ (β ≫ s.π) = 0 ∧ γ ≫ s.π = α ≫ β ≫ s.π := by
    intro s
    have hc : cmp χ γ α β ≫ s.π = 0 := s.condition
    have h1 := coprod.inl (X := free (R := R) m) (Y := free (R := R) Iγ) ≫= hc
    have h2 := coprod.inr (X := free (R := R) m) (Y := free (R := R) Iγ) ≫= hc
    rw [inl_cmp_assoc, comp_zero] at h1
    rw [inr_cmp_assoc, comp_zero, Preadditive.sub_comp, sub_eq_zero, Category.assoc] at h2
    exact ⟨h1, h2⟩
  have hfac : ∀ s : CokernelCofork (cmp χ γ α β),
      φ ≫ hcolim.desc (CokernelCofork.ofπ (β ≫ s.π) (key s).1) = β ≫ s.π := fun s =>
    hcolim.fac (CokernelCofork.ofπ (β ≫ s.π) (key s).1) WalkingParallelPair.one
  have hmain : ∀ s : CokernelCofork (cmp χ γ α β),
      ψ ≫ hcolim.desc (CokernelCofork.ofπ (β ≫ s.π) (key s).1) = s.π := by
    intro s
    refine (cancel_epi γ).mp ?_
    rw [← Category.assoc γ ψ, ← hα, Category.assoc α φ, hfac s]
    exact (key s).2.symm
  refine Cofork.IsColimit.mk _ (fun s => hcolim.desc (CokernelCofork.ofπ (β ≫ s.π) (key s).1))
    hmain fun s mm hmm => ?_
  change ψ ≫ mm = s.π at hmm
  exact hψ.left_cancellation _ _ (by rw [hmm, hmain s])

include hχφ hα hβ in
/-- **Stacks 01BP, local form.** If `F` is presented by `free m --χ--> free n --φ--> F`, if `A`
is generated by `free Iγ` via `γ`, and if `ψ : A ⟶ F` admits comparison maps `α` and `β`
against the presentation, then the kernel of `ψ` is generated by `m ⊕ Iγ` sections. When `m`
and `Iγ` are finite this family is finite, which is what Stacks 01BP asserts locally. -/
noncomputable def generatingSectionsKernel
    (hcolim : IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ φ hχφ)) [Epi γ] [Epi φ] :
    (kernel ψ).GeneratingSections where
  I := m ⊕ Iγ
  s := (kernel ψ).freeHomEquiv ((freeSumIso m Iγ).inv ≫
    kernel.lift ψ (cmp χ γ α β) (cmp_comp χ γ α β φ ψ hχφ hα hβ))
  epi := by
    rw [Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
    have := epi_kernelLift_of_isColimit (cmp χ γ α β) ψ
      (cmp_comp χ γ α β φ ψ hχφ hα hβ) (isColimitCmp χ γ α β φ ψ hχφ hα hβ hcolim)
    infer_instance

/-- The generating family of `kernel ψ` produced by `generatingSectionsKernel` is finite as
soon as the relations of the presentation and the generators of `A` are. -/
instance isFiniteType_generatingSectionsKernel [Finite m] [Finite Iγ]
    (hcolim : IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ φ hχφ)) [Epi γ] [Epi φ] :
    (generatingSectionsKernel χ γ α β φ ψ hχφ hα hβ hcolim).IsFiniteType where
  finite := inferInstanceAs (Finite (m ⊕ Iγ))

end Cmp

/-! ### Stacks 01BP for a sheaf of modules with a global finite presentation -/

section Main

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C]
  {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ X : C, HasSheafify (J.over X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ X : C, (J.over X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : C, PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} (overFunctor.{u} R V)]

/-- Restriction of sheaves of modules to a slice site preserves limits of small shape, hence
kernels. This is `preservesLimitPushforward` stated for `SheafOfModules.overFunctor`, which is
a `def` and so is not seen by instance search. -/
noncomputable instance preservesLimitOverFunctor (V : C) {Kc : Type} [SmallCategory Kc]
    (G : Kc ⥤ SheafOfModules.{u} R) : PreservesLimit G (overFunctor.{u} R V) := by
  change PreservesLimit G (SheafOfModules.pushforward.{u} (𝟙 (R.over V)))
  infer_instance

/-- Global generating sections, read as local generators data for the trivial covering of the
site. This is Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.localGeneratorsData`, restated under
the hypothesis that restriction to a slice site preserves colimits instead of under
`HasBinaryProducts C`, which is only one way to obtain that. -/
noncomputable def localGeneratorsDataOfGeneratingSections {M : SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (G : M.GeneratingSections) : M.LocalGeneratorsData where
  I := C
  X := id
  coversTop _ := GrothendieckTopology.covering_of_eq_top J <| by simp
  generators V := G.map (overFunctor.{u} R V) (unitOverIso V)

/-- The comparison map `α` of the Stacks 01BP argument, assembled over `V` from local lifts of
the generators of the source through the presentation of the target. -/
noncomputable def alphaOf {n Iγ : Type u} (V : C)
    (τ : Iγ → (unit (R.over V) ⟶ (free (R := R) n).over V)) :
    free (R := R.over V) Iγ ⟶ free (R := R.over V) n :=
  (freeHomEquiv _).symm fun k => (free (R := R.over V) n).unitHomEquiv
    (τ k ≫ (mapFreeIso (overFunctor R V) n (unitOverIso V)).inv)

/-- `alphaOf` is a lift of the generating morphism of the source through the presentation. -/
lemma alphaOf_spec {n Iγ : Type u} {F G : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (θ : G ⟶ F) (V : C)
    (φ₀ : free (R := R) n ⟶ F) (γ₀ : free (R := R) Iγ ⟶ G)
    (τ : Iγ → (unit (R.over V) ⟶ (free (R := R) n).over V))
    (hτ : ∀ k, τ k ≫ φ₀.over V =
      (show unit (R.over V) ⟶ F.over V from (ιFree k ≫ γ₀ ≫ θ).over V)) :
    alphaOf (R := R) V τ ≫
        ((mapFreeIso (overFunctor R V) n (unitOverIso V)).hom ≫ φ₀.over V) =
      ((mapFreeIso (overFunctor R V) Iγ (unitOverIso V)).hom ≫ γ₀.over V) ≫ θ.over V := by
  refine free_hom_ext fun k => ?_
  simp only [Category.assoc, alphaOf, ιFree_freeHomEquiv_symm_assoc, Equiv.symm_apply_apply,
    Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc, ιFree_mapFreeIso_over_hom_assoc]
  rw [hτ k]
  exact (overFunctor R V).map_comp _ _

/-- The comparison map `β` of the Stacks 01BP argument, assembled over `V` from local lifts of
the presentation generators of the target through `θ`. -/
noncomputable def betaOf {n : Type u} {G : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (V : C)
    (υ : n → (unit (R.over V) ⟶ G.over V)) :
    free (R := R.over V) n ⟶ G.over V :=
  (freeHomEquiv _).symm fun l => (G.over V).unitHomEquiv (υ l)

/-- `betaOf` is a lift of the presentation of the target through `θ`. -/
lemma betaOf_spec {n : Type u} {F G : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (θ : G ⟶ F) (V : C)
    (φ₀ : free (R := R) n ⟶ F) (υ : n → (unit (R.over V) ⟶ G.over V))
    (hυ : ∀ l, υ l ≫ θ.over V =
      (show unit (R.over V) ⟶ F.over V from (ιFree l ≫ φ₀).over V)) :
    betaOf (R := R) V υ ≫ θ.over V =
      (mapFreeIso (overFunctor R V) n (unitOverIso V)).hom ≫ φ₀.over V := by
  refine free_hom_ext fun l => ?_
  simp only [betaOf, ιFree_freeHomEquiv_symm_assoc, Equiv.symm_apply_apply,
    ιFree_mapFreeIso_over_hom_assoc]
  rw [hυ l]
  exact (overFunctor R V).map_comp _ _

/-- Over an object `V` where the generators of `G` lift through the presentation of `F`, and
the presentation generators of `F` lift through `θ`, the restriction of `kernel θ` to the
slice site over `V` is generated by finitely many sections. -/
lemma exists_generatingSections_over {F G : SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (P : F.Presentation) [P.IsFinite] (gs : G.GeneratingSections) [gs.IsFiniteType]
    (θ : G ⟶ F) (V : C)
    (τ : gs.I → (unit (R.over V) ⟶ (free (R := R) P.generators.I).over V))
    (hτ : ∀ k, τ k ≫ (P.generators.π).over V =
      (show unit (R.over V) ⟶ F.over V from (ιFree k ≫ gs.π ≫ θ).over V))
    (υ : P.generators.I → (unit (R.over V) ⟶ G.over V))
    (hυ : ∀ l, υ l ≫ θ.over V =
      (show unit (R.over V) ⟶ F.over V from (ιFree l ≫ P.generators.π).over V)) :
    ∃ σ : ((kernel θ).over V).GeneratingSections, Finite σ.I := by
  set PV := P.map (overFunctor R V) (unitOverIso V) with hPV
  set gsV := gs.map (overFunctor R V) (unitOverIso V) with hgsV
  have hπP : PV.generators.π =
      (mapFreeIso (overFunctor R V) P.generators.I (unitOverIso V)).hom ≫
        (P.generators.π).over V := Presentation.map_π_eq _ _ _
  have hπg : gsV.π =
      (mapFreeIso (overFunctor R V) gs.I (unitOverIso V)).hom ≫ (gs.π).over V :=
    GeneratingSections.map_π_eq _ _ _
  have hα : alphaOf (R := R) V τ ≫ PV.generators.π = gsV.π ≫ θ.over V := by
    rw [hπP, hπg]; exact alphaOf_spec θ V _ _ τ hτ
  have hβ : betaOf (R := R) V υ ≫ θ.over V = PV.generators.π := by
    rw [hπP]; exact betaOf_spec θ V _ υ hυ
  have hχφ : ((freeHomEquiv _).symm PV.relations.s ≫ kernel.ι PV.generators.π) ≫
      PV.generators.π = 0 := by simp
  have h1 : Finite PV.relations.I := inferInstanceAs (Finite P.relations.I)
  have h2 : Finite gsV.I := inferInstanceAs (Finite gs.I)
  refine ⟨GeneratingSections.equivOfIso
    (PreservesKernel.iso (overFunctor R V) θ).symm
    (generatingSectionsKernel ((freeHomEquiv _).symm PV.relations.s ≫ kernel.ι PV.generators.π)
      gsV.π (alphaOf (R := R) V τ) (betaOf (R := R) V υ) PV.generators.π (θ.over V)
      hχφ hα hβ PV.isColimit), ?_⟩
  exact inferInstanceAs (Finite (PV.relations.I ⊕ gsV.I))

/-- **Stacks 01BP for a sheaf of modules with a global finite presentation.** If `F` admits a
finite presentation by global sections and `θ : G ⟶ F` is an epimorphism from a sheaf of
modules generated by finitely many global sections, then `Ker θ` is of finite type.

The covering family witnessing finite type consists of all objects `V` over which the
generators of `G` lift through the presentation of `F` and the presentation generators of `F`
lift through `θ`; `exists_lift_over_of_epi` says that each of these finitely many lifting
conditions holds on a covering sieve, and `iInf_mem` intersects them. -/
theorem isFiniteType_kernel_of_presentation {F G : SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (P : F.Presentation) [P.IsFinite] (gs : G.GeneratingSections) [gs.IsFiniteType]
    (θ : G ⟶ F) [Epi θ] : (kernel θ).IsFiniteType := by
  classical
  have hcover : J.CoversTop (Subtype.val :
      { V : C // ∃ σ : ((kernel θ).over V).GeneratingSections, Finite σ.I } → C) := by
    intro Y
    choose S₁ hS₁ hlift₁ using fun k : gs.I =>
      exists_lift_over_of_epi P.generators.π (ιFree k ≫ gs.π ≫ θ) Y
    choose S₂ hS₂ hlift₂ using fun l : P.generators.I =>
      exists_lift_over_of_epi θ (ιFree l ≫ P.generators.π) Y
    refine J.superset_covering ?_
      (J.intersection_covering (iInf_mem J _ hS₁) (iInf_mem J _ hS₂))
    intro V g hg
    obtain ⟨hg₁, hg₂⟩ := hg
    rw [iInf_apply] at hg₁ hg₂
    choose τ hτ using fun k => hlift₁ k g (hg₁ k)
    choose υ hυ using fun l => hlift₂ l g (hg₂ l)
    exact (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff _ g).2
      ⟨⟨V, exists_generatingSections_over P gs θ V τ hτ υ hυ⟩, ⟨𝟙 V⟩⟩
  exact ⟨⟨{ I := { V : C // ∃ σ : ((kernel θ).over V).GeneratingSections, Finite σ.I }
            X := Subtype.val
            coversTop := hcover
            generators := fun i => i.2.choose }, ⟨fun i => ⟨i.2.choose_spec⟩⟩⟩⟩

/-- **Stacks 01BP, part (1), for a sheaf of modules with a global finite presentation.** If `F`
admits a finite presentation by global sections and `ψ : free I ⟶ F` is an epimorphism from a
finite-rank free sheaf of modules, then `Ker ψ` is of finite type. -/
theorem isFiniteType_kernel_free_of_presentation {F : SheafOfModules.{u} R}
    (P : F.Presentation) [P.IsFinite] {I : Type u} [Finite I] (ψ : free I ⟶ F) [Epi ψ] :
    (kernel ψ).IsFiniteType :=
  have : (free.generatingSections (R := R) I).IsFiniteType := ⟨inferInstanceAs (Finite I)⟩
  isFiniteType_kernel_of_presentation P (free.generatingSections I) ψ

end Main

end Stacks.SheafOfModules.FiniteTypeKernel

end
